<title>BELGIUM: TNT Express wins Walloon region aid, concessions.</title>
<headline>TNT Express wins Walloon region aid, concessions.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLEROI, Belgium 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Courier group GD Express Worldwide, which operates as TNT Express Worldwide, won 525 million Belgian francs in regional aid on Thursday for its Liege air hub project, the Walloon regional government said. Furthermore, the company was allowed to carry out accelerated depreciation on its 2.16 billion franc investment and was granted a real estate tax waiver.</p>
<p>The air hub, to be opened in 1998, will create 300 new jobs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
